The cache premise also splits by provider. The installed adapter explicitly marks Anthropic cache breakpoints on the system prompt, last tool definition, and last user content. Its Google adapter sends no `cachedContent` handle at all; any Gemini benefit therefore depends on Google’s implicit caching for the selected model, not on a pi-managed stable prefix. I’m verifying model eligibility, minimums, TTL, and invalidation against current provider docs before assigning value to #6/#12.
